\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. A Virgin most pure, as the prophets do tell,
\par Hath brought forth a Baby, as it hath befel,
\par To be our Redeemer from death, hell, and sin,
\par Which Adam's transgression hath wrapped us in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And therefore be merry, set sorrow aside;
\par Christ Jesus our Saviour was born on this tide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In Bethlehem in Jewry, a city there was
\par Where Joseph and Mary together did pass,
\par All for to be taxed with many one moe,
\par For Caesar commanded the same should be so.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And therefore be merry, set sorrow aside;
\par Christ Jesus our Saviour was born on this tide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But when they had entered the city so fair,
\par A number of people so mighty was there,
\par That Joseph and Mary, whose substance was small,
\par Could find in the inn there no lodging at all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And therefore be merry, set sorrow aside;
\par Christ Jesus our Saviour was born on this tide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then were they constrained in a stable to lie,
\par Where horses and asses they used for to tie:
\par Their lodging so simple they took it no scorn,
\par But against the next morning our Saviour was born.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And therefore be merry, set sorrow aside;
\par Christ Jesus our Saviour was born on this tide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The King of all kings to this world being brought,
\par Small store of fine linen to wrap Him was sought,
\par But when she had swaddled her young son so sweet,
\par Within an ox-manger she laid Him to sleep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And therefore be merry, set sorrow aside;
\par Christ Jesus our Saviour was born on this tide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Then God sent an angel from heaven so high,
\par To certain poor shepherds in fields where they lie,
\par And bade them no longer in sorrow to stay,
\par Because that our Saviour was born on this day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And therefore be merry, set sorrow aside;
\par Christ Jesus our Saviour was born on this tide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Then presently after the shepherds did spy
\par A number of angels that stood in the sky;
\par They joyfully talked and sweetly did sing,
\par To God be all glory, our heavenly King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And therefore be merry, set sorrow aside;
\par Christ Jesus our Saviour was born on this tide.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

